    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0486" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-24T22:00:00-05:00">June 24, 1938—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. For the Under Secretary of State. Tentative agreement reached today between
                        Crafts,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d481-f1"/> Brownson and Pujol for settlement
                    of Warren Brothers obligations at 80 and port notes at 60 in the new emission of
                    bonds, and also of Purdy, Henderson claim as per previous agreement at 80 in
                    both 85 million dollars issue, all subject to Government ratification. Pujol
                    appears confident of his ability to obtain Government ratification. Crafts will
                    be informed on Tuesday next of Government decision when Brownson settlement
                    seems assured.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d481-f1" n="16" xml:id="d481-f1-content">
                <p>Frederick A. Crafts, senior counsel for Warren Brothers Co.</p>
            </note>
